 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Definitely. Lots of laptops now have backlights that you can turn off completely. If you do that, a simple piece of paper with a window cut into it gives plenty of light. Stick it in your pocket between layers and it stays dry. If you do a lot of reading on public transport, it' worth it. Some brands make them without a track ball altogether, and they' much cleaner. If you can get one of those, it' worth switchering. On keyboards, a compact one is much cleaner. Many manufacturers now give left handed models as options, so it' worth checking. If not, you can sometimes swap the keys around with a little tool that comes with most new keyboards.",
